  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT17-081#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT17-081 (Sep. 6, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, that's correct.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's [All Turns] effect to gain 2 memory if I have a Digimon with [Greymon] and a Digimon with [Garurumon]?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  Even if the played Digimon is removed before the effect activates, it triggers because the \"when [...] Digimon is played\" condition is met, then the effect can activate. However, the \"if you have a Digimon with [XX]\" condition is no longer met once the Digimon is removed, therefore you don't gain 1 memory.",
        "question": "When I play a Digimon with [Greymon], then its DP becomes 0 and is deleted upon play due to a persistent effect, can I activate this card's [All Turns] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  This card's [End of Your Turn] effect does not allow you to attack with Digimon that are in a state where they can't attack.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's [End of Your Turn] effect to attack using my Digimon with [Omnimon] even when it's suspended?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  If BT5-086 [Omnimon] digivolves during the main phase, you can use the [End of Your Turn] effect to attack again after the attack from ＜Blitz＞ ends.",
        "question": "I attacked using BT5-086 [Omnimon]'s ＜Blitz＞ and unsuspended it using the other [When Digivolving] effect. After the attack ends, can I use this card's [End of Your Turn] effect to attack again?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  The effect will trigger on both copies, but after the attack declaration is made for the 1st [Omnimon] and effects such as [When Attacking] effects have finished activating, the effect on the 2nd copy of this card that was pending activation will activate before the counter timing. However, a new attack declaration can't be made during an attack, and only the 1st [Omnimon]'s attack can be performed as a result.",
        "question": "When I have 2 copies of this Tamer and 2 unsuspended Digimon with [Omnimon], can I activate the [End of Your Turn] effect on both copies of this card and attack using both of the Digimon with [Omnimon]?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
